1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,748
What if you could run an Oracle APEX app without an Oracle database?

2
00:00:05,008 --> 00:00:08,745
No instance, no workspace, no import. Just your laptop.

3
00:00:09,895 --> 00:00:14,245
APEXREST runs APEXlang sources locally, on Node.js.

4
00:00:14,505 --> 00:00:21,455
Pages use the genuine Universal Theme 26.2 templates and Oracle's own JavaScript.

5
00:00:21,715 --> 00:00:26,064
SQLite stands in for the database, with Oracle SQL shims.

6
00:00:27,214 --> 00:00:30,864
To put it to the test, we built a 22-page showcase app.

7
00:00:31,124 --> 00:00:34,485
Every page targets one family of APEX components.

8
00:00:35,635 --> 00:00:40,107
Classic reports with sorting, pagination and alternative templates.

9
00:00:40,367 --> 00:00:44,989
Interactive reports with saved reports, Group By, Pivot and Chart views.

10
00:00:45,249 --> 00:00:49,787
Editable interactive grids that save through Automatic Row Processing.

11
00:00:50,937 --> 00:00:54,042
Modal forms open in a real APEX dialog.

12
00:00:54,302 --> 00:00:59,061
The server validates the submit and errors appear inline, just like in APEX.

13
00:01:00,211 --> 00:01:04,015
The item gallery puts 57 page items on one page.

14
00:01:04,275 --> 00:01:09,597
Date pickers, popup LOVs, shuttles, switches, star ratings, uploads and more.

15
00:01:10,747 --> 00:01:13,695
Faceted search filters cards with live counts.

16
00:01:13,955 --> 00:01:18,555
Smart filters, list views and template components work over the same data.

17
00:01:19,705 --> 00:01:24,178
The dashboard has sixteen charts, drawn by a local SVG renderer.

18
00:01:24,438 --> 00:01:28,123
Bars, lines, donuts, bubbles, funnels, radar and gauges.

19
00:01:29,273 --> 00:01:32,126
Calendars with month, week, day and list views.

20
00:01:32,386 --> 00:01:37,792
Trees from CONNECT BY queries, and maps with points, lines, polygons and heat layers.

21
00:01:38,942 --> 00:01:42,380
Dynamic actions react in the browser and call the server.

22
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:48,430
Processes and validations run in a PL/SQL interpreter, with rollback on error.

23
00:01:48,690 --> 00:01:51,771
Collections, mail and REST calls are answered locally.

24
00:01:52,921 --> 00:01:56,125
Multi-step wizards, file upload and download,

25
00:01:56,385 --> 00:02:02,132
and the Universal Theme gallery: alerts, tabs, carousels, buttons and inline dialogs.

26
00:02:03,282 --> 00:02:08,132
preview check renders all 22 pages: zero errors, zero warnings.

27
00:02:08,392 --> 00:02:12,650
Whatever it cannot simulate is listed in diagnostics, never hidden.

28
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,539
So what does running APEXlang locally give you?

29
00:02:16,799 --> 00:02:19,813
Design feedback in seconds, not after an import.

30
00:02:20,073 --> 00:02:24,974
No database or shared workspace: it runs on a laptop, even offline.

31
00:02:25,234 --> 00:02:30,188
Safe experiments: data lives in local SQLite and resets anytime.

32
00:02:30,448 --> 00:02:34,065
And AI agents can open and click the pages they write.

33
00:02:35,215 --> 00:02:41,394
It is a design aid, not Oracle evidence: you still validate and import on real APEX.

34
00:02:41,654 --> 00:02:45,476
APEXREST is open source. Try the local preview today.

